Before WebRTC existed:

Video calling in browsers required plugins like Flash or Java Applets.
Applications such as Skype required separate software installation.
Plugins introduced security risks and compatibility issues.

To solve these problems, companies like Google, Mozilla, and Opera developed WebRTC.

The main goals were:

✅ Plugin-free communication
✅ Secure communication
✅ Low-latency real-time communication
✅ Cross-browser support